NOTICE OF MODIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a derived work and is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by
Anthropic. Do not report issues with this project to Anthropic.

Substantial modifications have been made to every component of the original.
Summarized:

  * Measurement correctness. The original's aggregation, trigger-evaluation, and
    grading paths could each return a well-formed, plausible result computed from
    no data — an all-zero benchmark from a valid workspace, a trigger score from
    probes that never ran, a token column derived from character counts. These
    paths now either report a data-backed number or fail loudly.

  * A single canonical workspace layout, reconciled across the producing
    workflow, the aggregator, the review viewer, and the grading validator, which
    previously disagreed with one another in ways that produced silent zeros.

  * Cross-platform file I/O and console handling throughout. The original read
    and wrote at the platform default encoding in roughly thirty places, which on
    Windows corrupted skill descriptions silently and crashed several entry points
    outright.

  * Target-aware frontmatter validation. The original enforced one key set as
    universal and rejected a majority of the skills shipped in Anthropic's own
    marketplace. Validation is now explicit about which target it is checking.

  * Packaging no longer includes .env files, version-control directories, virtual
    environments, or symlink targets from outside the source tree, and emits a
    format that installable surfaces actually accept.

  * Per-probe isolation and spend controls for the description-optimization loop,
    which previously wrote into the user's live configuration directory and had no
    bound on cost.

  * Restructured and substantially rewritten SKILL.md and sub-agent prompts, plus
    new reference documentation on skill loading behavior, frontmatter targets,
    and distribution routes.

Original authorship of the underlying design and of the surviving portions
remains with Anthropic, PBC.
